hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23041","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Qays, on the authority of al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Muslims whose four children die except Allah admits them to Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and three? He said: And three. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. And among my ummah is one who will loom large for the Fire until he becomes one of its corners, and among my ummah is one through whose intercession more than Mudar will enter Paradise."
